  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compare the probability of the maximum outcome: A has a 33% chance of 2500 Euros, B has a 100% chance of 2400 Euros. The reason would prefer B because 100% > 33%. However, the individual does not mention the probability of the maximum outcome at all. Instead, the individual focuses on the risk of losing everything (the 1% chance of 0 in A) and whether the gains are large enough to justify that risk. This is a different reasoning process — one based on risk aversion and gain size — not on the probability of the maximum outcome. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information relevant to the reason is absent from the report, and the justification does not reflect the rule of the reason. The individual’s reasoning is unrelated to the probability of the maximum outcome. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

